# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere — index and worktree, every box.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalizes every text file to LF on commit AND checks
# out LF on every platform. The `eol` attribute beats `core.autocrlf` for
# checkout conversion, so Windows clones get LF worktrees (matching Linux CI)
# without per-machine config. The pre-commit hook reads worktree bytes, so
# this is what lets `yamllint new-lines` pass locally instead of only in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary media: never convert, never diff, never gate. (PNG/ICO headers
# carry `\r` bytes; without this git could misread them as text.)
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
